<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sappi half year earnings slide.</title>
<headline>Sappi half year earnings slide.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		16	    vs 215</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 nil	   vs 70</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts for earnings in the six months to March 31 were in a range of 10 to 40 cents with the consensus figure coming in at 27.5 cents and the dividend was seen at best being cut and at worst scrapped. The range was nil to 50 with a consensus figure of 23.3.</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   20.2	  vs 62.2</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   79.0	  vs 476.2</p>
<p>    Tax			 27.3	  vs 57.7</p>
<p>    Finance costs paid    568.1	 vs 463.0</p>
<p>    Finance costs capitalised 173.1   vs 144.3</p>
<p>    Turnover		  7,157.0     vs 6,597.6</p>
<p>Full name: Sappi Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Sappi is a pulp and paper producer.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
